From: EglantinePS5 <Vampinity@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: up: L1161 draw, checked handle words and vertex formats keep draw reuse (EDEN_UP_L1161_DRAW)

DRAFT, not built. Ports the remaining draw work of zortos293/Lichii PR #1161 (@lucastaonline,
e05a72847e and 792e12a47b), on 0557 and 0558. Gated by EDEN_UP_L1161_DRAW (exact 1), a live
switch (Id L1161Draw, not armed); off by default. Does something only with EDEN_UP_FAST_DRAW=1.
Computed handle programs are evaluated again under both cache locks (only a capture taken with
the switch on permits reuse); a write that reaches a handle buffer is compared word by word,
secondary array words included; dynamic vertex formats keep the pipeline's attribute type check;
range overflow widens conservatively and forbids uniform keeps. Adds "computed" and "vertex" to
the full counts of the 10-second fast draw line (0557).

Reviewed draft from job J, v2: reviewer re-anchored the live_switch.h hunks, made
TakeReusableDraw check the whole buffer with the cached spans first and translate single handle
words (separate handle_word_spans) only when a write reached the buffer, allocated the
per-pipeline handle word table on the first capture with the switch on (was ~2 KB per pipeline
always), and prefixed the ComputedHandleKind enumerators.
